    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 8:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "However, the LORD would not destroy Judah, for David his servant’s sake, as he promised him to give to him a lamp for his children always."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 8:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Joram slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David’s city; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his place."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 9:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "His servants carried him in a chariot to Jerusalem, and buried him in his tomb with his fathers in David’s city."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 11:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "The priest delivered to the captains over hundreds the spears and shields that had been King David’s, which were in the LORD’s house."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 12:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "For Jozacar the son of Shimeath, and Jehozabad the son of Shomer, his servants, struck him, and he died; and they buried him with his fathers in David’s city; and Amaziah his son reigned in his place."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, yet not like David his father. He did according to all that Joash his father had done."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "They brought him on horses, and he was buried at Jerusalem with his fathers in David’s city."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Azariah slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in David’s city; and Jotham his son reigned in his place."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:38",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jotham slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David’s city; and Ahaz his son reigned in his place."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 16:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ahaz was twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. He didn’t do that which was right in the LORD his God’s eyes, like David his father."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 16:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ahaz slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David’s city; and Hezekiah his son reigned in his place."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 17:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "For he tore Israel from David’s house; and they made Jeroboam the son of Nebat king; and Jeroboam drove Israel from following the LORD, and made them sin a great sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 18:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, according to all that David his father had done."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 19:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "‘For I will defend this city to save it, for my own sake and for my servant David’s sake.’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Turn back, and tell Hezekiah the prince of my people, ‘The LORD, the God of David your father, says, “I have heard your prayer. I have seen your tears. Behold, I will heal you. On the third day, you will go up to the LORD’s house."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "I will add to your days fifteen years. I will deliver you and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria. I will defend this city for my own sake, and for my servant David’s sake.”’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 21:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "He set the engraved image of Asherah that he had made in the house of which the LORD said to David and to Solomon his son, “In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will put my name forever;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 22:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, and walked in all the ways of David his father, and didn’t turn away to the right hand or to the left."
      }
    ],
